course: dictionary
lesson: 15416
title: Squish and squishy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Squish is a fun, everyday word. Its main meaning is to squash something soft, so that it gets flat or out of shape. «Sam sat on the sponge and squished it flat.» The sponge did not break into bits. It just went flat, so squish is about soft things.
explain: Squish can also describe a sound. «Ellie's boots squished in the muddy field.» Mud is soft and wet, so walking through it makes a squelchy, wet sound. Ask yourself: is the thing soft? If it is, squish may fit.
explain: Squish can be a noun too, naming the sound or feeling. «I felt a squish under my foot.» Squishy comes from the same family and means soft: a squishy cushion gives when you press it. Squish up is a phrase that means make room on a seat, so a friend can sit down next to you.
fact: Squish is a verb: squish, squishes, squished, squishing.
fact: «Squish» means to squash something soft so that it gets flat or out of shape.
fact: «Squishy» means soft, like a squishy sponge or a squishy bed.
fact: «Squish up» means make room on a seat, as in «Squish up, there is room for me!»
fact: Squish is informal, so you use it in chatty talk and play, not in a formal letter.
exercise: «Sam squished the soft sponge with his hand.» What does squished mean? | Lifted high above his head | Washed in cold water | Cut into small pieces | *Squashed so it went flat
exercise: «Ellie's boots squished in the muddy field.» What does squish describe here? | A cold wind blowing | *A soft, wet sound as she walked | A loud bang like a firework | A bright colour on the grass
exercise: Nadia says, «Squish up, there is room for me!» What does squish up mean? | Shout loudly at a friend | Squash a bug on the wall | Stand up and leave the room | *Move closer together to make room on a seat
test: «The cushion was squishy and soft.» What does squishy mean? | Very heavy | Shiny and bright | *Soft, so it gives when pressed | Hard and cold
test: «I felt a squish under my foot.» In this sentence, what kind of word is squish? | *A noun, a name for the sound or feeling | A question word | An interjection, a shout | A verb, a doing word
exam: «Mum squished the clay into a ball, and it went flat and soft.» Which word is closest in meaning to squished? | Painted | Forgot | Dropped | *Pressed
